#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "28 new identities to earn: Bastion, Warfather, Sun Incarnate, The Unseen, Voice of Fate, Wild Sovereign, King in Bone and more - each with its own passive creed and signature skill that supersedes the last"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A BOARD ON THE SQUARE: a notice board by the square lists what Pixelheim needs; Mayor Aldric now talks before he opens his books"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A CAT, A DOG AND TWO CHILDREN: Pixelheim has a cat that judges you, a dog that leans on you, and - once it's a village - Pip and Nell running about the square"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A DAWN YOU WATCH: when Maren has the letter, the Night of Ash ends on the town itself. The camera drifts from the shrine across Pixelheim as the fires gutter out one by one and the red night greys toward morning; the survivors stand together on the square and speak in their own voices - Maren, the mayor out of his hall, Bram and Sela beside you - and when Fafnyr is named, he roars, and his shadow sweeps over the town. Then the day begins: Pixelheim, day one"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A Dawn You Watch"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A FAVICON OF ITS OWN: the title's gold P under the moon, in your browser tab and on your home screen"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A FIFTH RANK: level 20 crowns the hero - Ironlord, Starcaller, Nightlord, Hierophant, Eldwarden, Exemplar or Deathlord - with an amethyst aura and a bonus skill point"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A FIRST BREW: Vex's quest now asks you to brew your first health potion at her cauldron"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A FIRST JOB AT THE FORGE: the Reedwoven Buckler takes 3 marsh reeds at Smithing 1, the Iron Helm opens at Smithing 2, and Scaled Mail needs one dragon scale, not two"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A FIRST NIGHT YOU CAN SKIP: hero creation has a First night toggle (Tab) for players who have walked it before"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A Fair Fight"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A Fresh Coat"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A Game's Face"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A HERO PLATE: your portrait, pixel bars for health, mana and experience, your gold, and each screen one click or key away"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A HOME IN THE SAME HAND: the rug, planter, bookshelf, banner, candelabra and bench you place at home are drawn like the rest of the village, the rug actually shows, and a bed's foot is the bed - rest there, but nothing can be set on it"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A HOME WORTH HAVING: a night in your own bed leaves you well rested (+10% XP for your next 30 fights), and furniture now helps where it stands - a bookshelf for XP, a banner for critical blows, candles for energy, a rug for gold, a plant for stronger potions, a bench for longer rest. The Manor's garden grows herbs and reeds for the cauldron"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A Home Worth Having"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A LEVEL IS A LIFT, NOT A REFILL: levelling up heals half your HP and mana instead of all of it, and brings 3 stat points instead of 5"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A LOADING SCREEN THAT IS THE GAME: the web build loads behind the title's own night sky, with the bar where the menu will appear"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A LOOT CURVE WORTH CHASING: the mountain's floors drop by how deep they are, so every band of floors is a step up - the Obsidian Blade waits on the last floors, and Dragonbane's hoard (now 23 damage) is no longer a step down. Gear drops more often, and a boss always drops a piece"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A LUTE AND A VAULT: Loras wants his lute back from a Deepwood troll, and Mirelle wants two gems for her vault's first shelf - no more paying them to move"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A Little Night Music"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A MAP IN A FRAME: unexplored ground shows as night, waypoints as cards you can travel from"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A NAME CUT IN GOLD: PIXELHEIM in deep gold letters that catch the light, over a menu of words chosen in gold - point with the mouse or use the keys"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A NEW FACE FOR EVERY SCREEN: parchment pages in carved wooden frames with brass studs, ink on the page, rubric red for whatever has your attention, and wooden planks for buttons that light brass when chosen"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A NEW LOOK FOR EVERY SCREEN: pixel-art windows on the title's night sky, pixel fonts drawn at whole sizes, gold for whatever has focus, keycaps for every key"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A NIGHT IN PIXELHEIM: the title opens on the village street after dark - lit windows, smoking chimneys, torches, the fountain, and the watchman on his round with his lantern"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A New Engine"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A PROPER BEGINNING: a new hero no longer just appears in town. You are a courier carrying a letter to Elder Maren, and you arrive on the road the night Pixelheim burns"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A REAL VILLAGE: the dirt road from the north gate opens into a paved square held by the shrine - market pockets, scalloped corners, the old well off its SW edge - with Main Street up top and a south lane serving every door"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A SAFER MIREFEN AND DEEPWOOD: the Mirefen's mimic pack is gone (its trapped chest waits in the far west, by Grandmother Gulp), and the Deepwood's trolls no longer stand at its gate"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A SHIELD OF REEDS: Hilda has a job for you too - weave a Reedwoven Buckler at her forge, and keep it"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A STORY TO FOLLOW: Pixelheim now has a main quest in three chapters - Under the Mountain, The Ashen Throne and The Deathless - from Sela's first job to Morvax's throne"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A Satchel of Icons"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A TELL BEFORE THE BITE: monsters flash before they bite, and the bite misses if you step away in time"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A TIDIER PACK: each row shows an item's name and numbers, the chosen one's whole description waits under the list, and empty slots on the paper doll show a faint outline of what goes there"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A TRADER IN EVERY REGION: Marta the Chandler in Saltmere, Quartermaster Brann at the Blackiron camp, Mabel the Sutler by Greyhold's road, and Gunnar's caravan on the Frostgate pass - each with their own pack and one rare piece"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A Tidy Pack"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A Village by Design"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A WEIGHT BAR: how full the pack is sits beside the weight, and it turns red near the limit"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A code-quality pass under the floorboards: one panel system instead of seven scattered flags - menus are properly modal everywhere now, and a save taken with any panel open loads clean"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A dozen new items: bows, war hammers, wands, cloaks, tower shields..."
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A hero from before keeps everything: whoever has cleared a floor finds the gate open, and Maren goes straight to her next ask"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A live stats panel beside the doll: ATK, DEF and every granted bonus, updating as you dress"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A lost fight still wakes you tucked into the inn's bed"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A mini-map rides in the corner of the world, fog included"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A path is a permanent identity: an always-on passive theme and a SIGNATURE SKILL no tree can teach"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A real sun wheels over the world: dawn light, long dusk shadows, and true darkness answered by lamplight, door glow and hearth fire"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A settler with something to ask still heals you or plays first, then asks"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A small-screen pass: panels fit, the HUD compacts, and nothing overlaps at any width"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "ALWAYS KNOW WHAT'S NEXT: a quiet line above the dock names your next step, and steps aside in fights and menus"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "AMBER WINDOWS that glow: honey-lit by day, warm lanterns down every street at night"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "AN HONEST BANK: Mirelle's savings now pay half a percent a day on what's in the pot, up to a tenth of it in all, and the interest is kept apart - topping up no longer folds it in or restarts the clock, so a pot can't be grown without end. The bank shows what your savings have earned so far, and there's a Deposit all"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "AN OWNER'S PERKS: you pay a tenth less in a shop you own, and its shelf keeps an owner's pick that changes every day"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "ANY WAY UP: the game fills a phone's screen held sideways or upright instead of sitting in a letterbox, the dock along the bottom and the pages in the middle. Upright, the art stays big enough to see the hero; sideways reads best, and the game says so once"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "ARMOUR SETS, READ RIGHT: a set's line now shows what each tier adds up to (five pieces of Oilskin give +5 DEX, not +3), the Greyhold Warden set guards a little better than the Blackiron that comes before it, and the shop says which stat a weapon hits with"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "ARMOUR SETS: pieces of one set worn together give more - at three pieces and again at five. The bonus shows on every piece (what you wear of it, what more would give) and on the stats page"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "ARMOUR TURNS ASIDE A SHARE: armour no longer subtracts a flat amount from each hit, it turns aside a share of it. More armour always helps, each point a little less than the last, and no hero is ever immune - a warrior in Blackiron at the gate takes about a third of a hit, not 1. The stat sheet shows how much of a hit of your level your DEF turns aside"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "ARMS THAT WORK: each stride pumps the striding side's hand, and held gear rides it - the sword swings with the arm now, in 2D and voxel alike"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "ASK THE ELDER: Elder Maren and Mayor Aldric now end every conversation with what you should do next"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "ASKED BEFORE BIG BUYS: the house deed and the workbench ask before they take your gold - press again to buy. Furniture never blocks the doorway, an upgrade hands back what stood in its way, and new hints explain the house, deeds and the bank"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Alchemy learns to brew doubles; Foraging finds more, and finds pairs"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "All Three Phases"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Also: the town gate moved to the north wall - no more door ping-pong when holding a key"
msgstr ""

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Ambushes feel like ambushes: the monster lunges in, the screen shakes, !"
msgstr ""

